# Paths a scan of this repository skips. The tree deliberately carries
# thousands of secret-shaped and PII-shaped values as test data, and scanning
# them buries any real finding under self-inflicted noise.
#
# Who reads this file: the folder scans (`aka scan`, the dashboard's Scan page,
# `/aka:scan`) and the worktree scan the plugins' background sync runs. The
# per-prompt hooks do not — prompts, tool input, tool output and history
# backfill are scanned whatever this file says. Patterns are relative to this
# directory, and a scan aimed at a subdirectory does not read this file at all,
# so scan from the repository root.
#
# Matches are HARD-SKIPPED: the file is never read, so it yields no event and
# no finding. Every entry is anchored to the location it describes, so a
# directory of the same name somewhere else is still scanned.
#
# test/helpers/repo-akaignore.ts holds the guard both walkers that read this
# file run (packages/local-ops and packages/scanner): the set of tracked and
# planted files it skips must be exactly the set that guard names, and every
# entry here must change what is skipped.

# Detection-rule definitions and fixtures: each rule carries the exact patterns
# it targets in its `examples` and fixtures. GitHub secret scanning excludes
# the secret packs and every pack's fixtures under it
# (.github/secret_scanning.yml); this also skips the remaining rule
# definitions, which carry the same kind of examples.
/rules/

# Fixture data that lives under a package's `src/`: egress-extraction and
# posture samples, and the persistence sample datasets and corpus generator.
# Only test and bench files import them; no shipped module does.
/packages/detections/src/egress/fixtures/
/packages/detections/src/posture/fixtures/
/packages/persistence/src/test-fixtures/

# Constructed test fixtures: the shared adversarial corpus and each package's
# and tool's fixture tree.
/test/fixtures/
/packages/*/test/fixtures/
/tools/*/test/fixtures/
# The plugins' fixture trees stay scanned: they hold recordings of real
# sessions (payloads captured from a live Copilot CLI, Codex and Claude Code),
# which can carry real credentials, and the browser extension's tree is where
# raw web-chat captures (`*.har`, `*.raw.json`) are recorded before
# .gitignore keeps them out of git. The one constructed tree among them is the
# Copilot VS Code specimens, built from the published contract rather than
# recorded.
/plugins/copilot/test/fixtures/vscode-provisional/

# Benchmark suites and the corpora they generate.
/packages/*/bench/

# Gitignored build output. Each of these bundles inlines the detection packs,
# every rule's examples included.
/plugins/claude-code/scripts/
/plugins/codex/scripts/
/plugins/antigravity/scripts/
/plugins/copilot/scripts/
/plugins/claude-code/hooks/engine.js
/plugins/browser-extension/native-host/
# The CLI's packed copies of the same bundles, left behind by its `prepack`
# and by the standalone-binary staging.
/cli/native-host/
/cli/extension/
/cli/web-ui/
/cli/sea-dist/
/cli/dist-sea/

# TypeScript incremental build state: generated, and its content hashes read
# as high-entropy strings.
*.tsbuildinfo
